nistic style of their kings ... identifies them with the Graeco-Roman world." Punic was employed as the official language of the Numidian kingdom, as is shown by monumental inscriptions and coin legends.  Intellectual works also were written in Punic.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2492, 'temperature': 0.2})
